From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:58:05 -0400
Subject: feat: one setting gives every new Space its own session (issue 8)

GitHub issue 8 asked, after beta 5's essentials of a Space's own, for
every Space to be independent without turning Independent session on
Space by Space (BACKLOG S-274). "Give every new Space its own session"
in Settings -> Stedding -> Spaces (settings T29, sessions S35) writes
stedding.spaces.own_session, off by default:

- While it is on, a Space added to the profile's registry starts with a
  jar of its own, as Independent session turned on at once gives it
  (SpaceRegistry::Add); each Space's own switch still turns it off.
- Turned on with Spaces that still share the session, the page asks
  whether they should have their own too, naming how many and how many
  of their open pages would reload (the count sessions S10 asks with);
  "Turn On for All" turns each on, "New Spaces Only" leaves them.
- Turned off, it changes no Space: a new Space shares the session again
  and the others keep what they have (sessions S7).

Tests: SpaceRegistryTest.ANewSpaceTakesTheOwnSessionSetting,
SteddingPrefsTest.EveryPreferenceRegistersWithItsDefault (off), and
SettingsSpacesTest.EveryNewSpaceCanHaveItsOwnSession through the page.

Why: people who keep every Space apart (GitHub issue 8) had to turn the
session on in each Space, and again for every Space they added.
Removable when: never; it is a product setting.
